The attached image, Figure 7D, is an immunoblot demonstrating the molecular weight of secreted and intracellular IL-1β. It confirms that in bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs) primed with LPS, the inactive pro-IL-1β (∼30 kD) is present in cell lysates. More importantly, when BMDCs are stimulated with Nano-11, especially after LPS priming, the active, cleaved form of IL-1β (∼17 kD) is detected in the supernatant. This verifies that Nano-11 induces the processing and secretion of biologically active IL-1β, a crucial pro-inflammatory cytokine, which supports its role as an effective vaccine adjuvant by activating dendritic cells.